{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass at the end, etc.</b> One needs to know: from where did he know the time at which he could open the window of the ark, without concern for drowning in the waters lest harm befall them? Or perhaps he was assured that there would be no more than twelve months. Further, from the fact that he prepared food provisions — and presumably he prepared for a limited time — from this he knew the measure of how long he would be kept in the ark."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:40:08.460615804Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}